# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MEX sources and anything used to build them
#
# The compiled binaries are what ships -- the .mex files for each platform, and
# libfftw3-3.dll beside ringRm -- so the sources they are built from stay out of
# the repository. The patterns also cover build systems that are not in the tree
# today, so that adding one does not quietly commit it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.c
*.cpp
*.cc
*.cxx
*.cu
*.cuh
*.h
*.hpp
*.vcxproj
*.vcxproj.*
*.sln
Makefile
makefile
*.mk

# Build projects and source archives. MATLAB Coder .prj files generate the
# coilCombine mex; the .zip archives are the vendors' source distributions
# (bart, fftw). None of them is needed to run the app -- the compiled binaries
# beside them are -- so they stay local like the other build inputs.
*.prj
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build folders, excluded whole rather than by extension
#
#   unRing/OSX, unRing/Windows   ringRm.cpp and the fftw archives. What the app
#                                loads -- the four ringRm.mex files and
#                                libfftw3-3.dll -- sits outside them.
#   coilCombine/codegen          MATLAB Coder output. The four coilCombine.mex
#                                files the app loads sit outside it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
functions/unRing/OSX/
functions/unRing/Windows/
functions/coilCombine/codegen/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sources that ship as .p
#
# The rule: where a .p exists beside a .m, the .p is committed and the .m stays
# local. This list is generated from the tree -- regenerate it after p-coding a
# new source, or after moving one. An entry naming a file that has moved stops
# ignoring anything, and that source then gets committed by accident.
#
# NOTE: a .m listed here is NOT in the repository. Edits to it live only on this
# machine and in Dropbox, so a "git checkout" or "git restore" of a tracked file
# cannot bring them back -- Dropbox version history is the only copy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+proud/+io/exportDicomDCM.m
+proud/+io/exportDicomMRD.m
+proud/+io/exportGifProud.m
+proud/+io/exportNiftiFcn.m
